  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## No API Keys Required!\n",
    "\n",
    "One of the main benefits of using local models is that you don't need any API keys or internet connection for the LLM inference. Just make sure Ollama is running locally on `http://localhost:11434`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## fenic session with Local LLM\n",
    "Set up the session for fenic with a local model via LiteLLM as the LLM to use for semantic operations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import fenic as fc\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n",
    "from fenic.core._inference.model_catalog import ModelProvider\n",
    "from fenic._inference.litellm.litellm_batch_chat_completions_client import LiteLLMBatchChatCompletionsClient\n",
    "from fenic._inference.rate_limit_strategy import UnifiedTokenRateLimitStrategy\n",
    "\n",
    "# Configure session with local LLM capabilities\n",
    "config = fc.SessionConfig(\n",
    "    app_name=\"hello_debug_local\",\n",
    "    semantic=fc.SemanticConfig(\n",
    "        # No language_models config needed - we'll use the provider directly\n",
    "        default_language_model=\"local_qwen\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create session\n",
    "session = fc.Session.get_or_create(config)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Configure the local LLM client manually\n",
    "rate_limit_strategy = UnifiedTokenRateLimitStrategy(rpm=100, tpm=10000)  # Local models can handle higher rates\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create LiteLLM client for local inference\n",
    "litellm_client = LiteLLMBatchChatCompletionsClient(\n",
    "    rate_limit_strategy=rate_limit_strategy,\n",
    "    model=\"qwen3:30b\",  # Using the local Qwen3 30B model\n",
    "    queue_size=50,\n",
    "    max_backoffs=3,\n",
    "    api_base=\"http://localhost:11434\"  # Default Ollama endpoint\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Session configured with local LLM: qwen3:30b\")\n",
    "print(\"📍 Ollama endpoint: http://localhost:11434\")\n",
    "print(\"💰 Cost: $0.00 (local inference)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## About the Data\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset contains a collection of synthetic but realistic error logs from various microservices in a modern application stack. \n",
    "\n",
    "Each entry includes a timestamp, the service name, and a detailed error log message. \n",
    "\n",
    "The logs cover a range of issues such as exceptions, connection failures, timeouts, cache misses, slow queries, and more. \n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset is ideal for demonstrating error analysis, root cause extraction, and automated debugging workflows using semantic data tools."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-7",
   "metadata": {},
